# Vercel project with Root Directory `backend` (README "Deploy on Vercel"). Keeps secrets and dev files out of
# CLI uploads (git deploys never contain them: they are git-ignored). A denylist on purpose, not a `/*` allowlist:
# the build step reads ../amd/system1 (vercel_build.py), so nothing outside backend/ may be ignored by accident.
# vercel.json `excludeFiles` keeps tests and tooling out of the function bundle as well.
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key
.venv
venv
.pytest_cache
__pycache__
tests
